LTE modem stage 2 - WORK IN PROGRESS, NOT IN THE SERIES
(2026-09-24, docs/phase4-lte-modem-scoping.md "Stage 2")

Applies on top of kernel/patches/00*. Contents:
- pci_generic: qcom-sdx55m-flashless profile (channel map, 30-bit DMA),
  2 ms event polling timer (MSIs are lost), sets sbl_ee_from_reg and
  ev_polled.
- MHI core: mhi_poll_events(); SBL entry picked up from the EE register
  (sbl_ee_from_reg); handled event elements zeroed when polled; debug:
  "poll:" event logging and a BAD_TRE descriptor dump.
- mhi_sahara_modem (sahara-modem.c) and mhi_bl_logger (mhi-bl.c), from
  the Xiaomi Mi 10T postmarketOS port, adapted (image map, EFS from
  qcom/sdx55m-efs/, HELLO_RESP compatible version 1, per-packet and TX
  completion logging, SBL log printed line by line).
- qcom-sdx55-ctrl (on top of 0045): AP2MDM_STATUS claimed high at probe
  (it was driven low, telling the modem the host is not up).
- Kconfig: MHI_BUS_SAHARA_MODEM, MHI_BUS_BL_LOGGER (=y in the fragment).
- Last hunk (DTS, separate): EXPERIMENT dropping dma-coherent from &pcie2
  (intermittent BAD_TRE); no effect seen. The committed DTS keeps it.

Status: HELLO/HELLO_RESP done (TX completion OK), the SBL log ends at
"TRDATA Image Load, Start"; the modem then either rejects a queued
descriptor (BAD_TRE, completion code 0x11) or sends nothing.

 9 files changed, 858 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
